 own class while the first is silent. VACUITY: delete the roster and assert the same tree reports nothing at all, then leave a roster that will not parse and assert the same - absence is opt-out for the layer, and a rule that reddened every row on a malformed roster would punish the wrong file. COVERAGE NEVER GATES: assert a tree whose rows carry no Hat-Refs at all reports no finding and no advisory; once at least one row carries the cell, assert exactly one coverage advisory and no finding. THE DERIVED SET: assert effective_hats returns the union of a row's own refs with its SR parents', that a parent's change moves the child's answer with no child cell edited, and that a dangling SR-Refs contributes nothing rather than raising. Plus the anti-drift pin the second reader needs: assert trace's roster path equals hats.ROSTER_REL, since a test may import both modules where the shipped code may not.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies LLR-183's Hat-Refs provenance, name-resolution, severity and effective-set mechanics; SR-161's perspective-review acceptance is inspected by TC-211.\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"\"\"tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_an_undeclared_hat_name_is_a_finding; tests/test_trace_hats_driven.py::test_an_undeclared_hat_reds_a_real_run_under_strict; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_the_rule_is_vacuous_without_a_roster; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_an_unparseable_roster_is_vacuous_not_loud; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_coverage_is_one_advisory_and_never_a_finding; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_a_spine_that_uses_the_cell_nowhere_gets_NO_advisories; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_effective_hats_unions_the_parents; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_a_parent_re_ruling_moves_the_child_with_no_child_cell_edited; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_a_dangling_parent_contributes_nothing_rather_than_raising; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_the_roster_path_matches_the_hats_module; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_the_design_tier_is_checked_too_and_names_its_own_id; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_an_absent_roster_file_reads_as_no_names; tests/test_trace_hats.py::test_a_hat_no_row_is_attributable_to_is_reported\"\"\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\n\r\n\r\n[test.TC-198]\r\nverifies = [\"SR-161\", \"LLR-202\"]\r\nlevel = \"Unit\"\r\nmethod = \"\"\"Drive the arm over a real two-commit git repository whose HEAD holds an Approved SR-001 (and, for the tier case, an Approved LLR-001 and TC-001), with the change STAGED rather than committed - the hook's own question. FIRES: the requirement cell amended while Hat-Refs stands raises one finding naming the row and the moved cells, with the amendment arm firing alongside it so the second arm is proven an addition rather than a re-spelling. SILENT ON TRACED-ONLY MOVEMENT: writing the Hat-Refs cell itself - the perspective backfill's own edit - raises nothing, and neither does an SN-Refs re-point. SILENT WHEN DISCHARGED: substance and Hat-Refs moving together raises nothing here while the amendment arm still fires. VACUOUS WHERE THERE IS NO BASELINE, both shapes: a row minted in the staged commit, and a row amended below approval on both sides. STRUCTURALLY SILENT ON A TIER WITH NO SUCH COLUMN: an LLR and a TC amended in the same commit yield exactly one finding, the LLR's, so the scoping cannot pass by the arm being silent everywhere.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies the acceptance folded into LLR-202 (parent SR-161)\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"\"\"tests/test_trajectory_staged.py::test_amending_approved_cells_without_moving_hat_refs_warns; tests/test_trajectory_staged.py::test_hat_refs_arm_is_silent_when_only_traced_cells_move; tests/test_trajectory_staged.py::test_hat_refs_arm_is_silent_when_the_cell_moves_with_the_amendment; tests/test_trajectory_staged.py::test_hat_refs_arm_is_vacuous_where_a_row_has_no_baseline; tests/test_trajectory_staged.py::test_hat_refs_arm_is_silent_on_a_tier_that_carries_no_such_column\"\"\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\n\r\n\r\n[test.TC-211]\r\nverifies = [\"SR-161\", \"SR-186\"]\r\nlevel = \"Inspection\"\r\nmethod = \"Follow the decomposition proportionality inspection in docs/test/inspection-procedures.md#decomposition-proportionality-inspection; inspect one actual completed decomposition review record, its complete chain, and an extra paraphrasing child.\"\r\ntier = \"Release\"\r\nexpected = \"The actual review record names every applicable perspective's outcome, each child within a required tier has an independent decision or verification purpose, and the record explains why further splitting stops; any omitted outcome or purposeless child is an Inspection finding.\"\r\nautomated = \"No\"\r\nevidence = \"docs/test/inspection-procedures.md#decomposition-proportionality-inspection-result\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 5\r\ninputs = [\"docs/test/inspection-procedures.md\", \"SR-161\", \"SR-186\", \"docs/requirements/hats.toml\", \"docs/reviews/wi-976/016-ADJUDICATE-9d6ad4c.brief.md\", \"docs/reviews/wi-976/016-ADJUDICATE-9d6ad4c.md\"]\r\nmax_age = 90\r\nrubric = \"docs/rubrics/decomposition-proportionality.md\"\r\ntrigger = \"release\"\r\nmin_work_items = 10\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n[interface.IF-092]\r\nowner = \"scripts/wi_convert\"\r\nrequestors = [\"scripts/intake\"]\r\nchannel = \"call\"\r\ndata = \"wi_convert.COLUMNS (the 19-column row schema) and write_spec_file; ConvertError is the mint's refusal input\"\r\nversion = \"v1\"\r\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\n\r\n\r\n[interface.IF-023]\r\nowner = \"docs/work/\"\r\nconsumers = [\"scripts/check_trajectory\", \"external:downstream adopter\"]\r\nchannel = \"file\"\r\ndata = \"one Markdown spec per row; status is the directory\"\r\nversion = \"v3\"\r\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\r\ninterface_to_external = \"B-05\"\r\ncoincident = \"\"\"The format is what the adopter writes and every reader parses; a copy that reads as this format declares is the whole of what the seam delivers, and what the rows say is judged at their own tiers.\"\"\"\r\nnotes = \"\"\"Published contract, not a single consumer: at least 9 kit scripts walk the docs/work/ spec folder through the shared kitlib.registry/agent_common readers (check_trajectory, gen_trajectory, schedule, wi_convert, intake, dispatch, traj_panels, traj_status and more), and every downstream adopter's own WI registry is content they author - naming one reader would misstate the file's role. Ties to B-05 as the template's own delivered work-item format.\"\"\"\r\n\r\n\r\n[interface.IF-090]\r\nowner = \"scripts/intake\"\r\nrequestors = [\"scripts/integrate\", \"scripts/dispatch\", \"scripts/agent_loop\", \"scripts/adjudicate_act\", \"scripts/amendment_brief\"]\r\nchannel = \"call\"\r\ndata = \"merge intake, gap minting, advisory context, and adjudication-action policy\"\r\nversion = \"v1\"\r\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\n\r\n\r\n[interface.IF-078]\r\nowner = \"scripts/wi_convert\"\r\nrequestors = [\"scripts/plan_artifacts\"]\r\nchannel = \"call\"\r\ndata = \"wi_convert.write_spec_file with work_dir_for and spec_paths; ConvertError on a status the format has no directory for\"\r\nversion = \"v1\"\r\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\n\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
